      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To heighten the visceral contrast, you might describe Low-Tier skin as overly pale and translucent from artificial nutrient baths that strip away natural blood pigment, making them look like weeping ghosts compared to the High-Tier's vibrant, sun-spotted complexions. Their facial features could be intentionally \"roughened\" by industrial mineral dust that never fully rinses off, creating permanent bags under their eyes and a haggard, tired look that physically screams their servitude. Furthermore, they should huddle together in defensive, huddled clusters, constantly touching their own rough skin to remind each other of their shared fragility, whereas the High-Tier walk with confident, upright postures, heads held high to the sun.",
